{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumUniverses.FundamentalObject","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumUniverses.FundamentalObject","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FundamentalObject.snake_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FundamentalObject.snake_right","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/fundamental-object.lean#L43-L43","doc":"right snake (zig-zag) identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FundamentalObject.snake_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FundamentalObject.snake_left","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/fundamental-object.lean#L40-L40","doc":"left snake (zig-zag) identity: `(volume, coform)` is a duality `V ⊣ V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FundamentalObject.coform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FundamentalObject.coform","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/fundamental-object.lean#L38-L38","doc":"its adjoint coform `η : 𝟙 ⟶ V ⊗ V`, exhibiting self-duality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FundamentalObject.volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FundamentalObject.volume","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/fundamental-object.lean#L36-L36","doc":"the volume form `ε : V ⊗ V ⟶ 𝟙` — the categorical determinant `Λ²V → 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FundamentalObject.V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FundamentalObject.V","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/fundamental-object.lean#L34-L34","doc":"the fundamental object itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FundamentalObject.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FundamentalObject.mk","kind":"ctor","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/fundamental-object.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FundamentalObject","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FundamentalObject","kind":"structure","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/fundamental-object.lean#L25-L44","doc":"**Fundamental object.** A self-dual object `V` of a monoidal category\ntogether with a volume form `volume : V ⊗ V ⟶ 𝟙` (the categorical\ndeterminant `Λ²V → 𝟙`) and its adjoint `coform : 𝟙 ⟶ V ⊗ V`, satisfying\nthe two snake identities. Together `(volume, coform)` exhibit `V ⊣ V`, i.e.\n`V` is its own dual. The volume constraint pins the categorical dimension to\n`2`; abstractly `V` is the unique such simple object and tensor-generates\nthe category. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:fundamental-object","label":"def:fundamental-object","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/fundamental-object.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}